{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They are turned against me</b> — Some say: For in days of old, if terrors came upon me — 'my nobility pursued' [תרדף נדיבתי], he means my fortune, and its meaning is: my fortune pursued them like the wind of terrors, and drove them away, and 'my salvation passed' [תעבר ישועתי] to come to me, like a cloud, in swiftness."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:02.680520365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}